# SABOTAGE: T84b (RP-J-7 consumption, ADR-044 s5.2b). A k-anon-suppressed cohort cell
# (%{"suppressed"=>true, ...}) must render ONLY the opaque "⊘" glyph - never any of the
# wire-carried Suppressed struct detail (reason/k/l/observed/limit), which would leak internal
# floor/threshold information about the suppression to the operator. Interpolating the
# suppression "reason" into the rendered cell defeats that: the k-anon floor's internal detail
# now reaches the cockpit render. Positive control: a genuinely non-suppressed numeric value
# still renders correctly (untouched fallback clause).
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/fleet_detail_scope_mask_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: a %Suppressed{}-shaped cohort cell renders '⊘', never the underlying wire value
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/fleet_detail_live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/fleet_detail_live.ex
index 169af14..3990b6e 100644
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/fleet_detail_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/fleet_detail_live.ex
@@ -203,6 +203,6 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.Operator.FleetDetailLive do
     |> Enum.map_join(" · ", fn {k, v} -> "#{k}: #{suppressed_or(v)}" end)
   end
 
-  defp suppressed_or(%{"suppressed" => true}), do: "⊘"
+  defp suppressed_or(%{"suppressed" => true, "reason" => reason}), do: "⊘ (#{reason})"
   defp suppressed_or(v), do: to_string(v)
 end
